  [ [=[If the humans are the masters of the age, then their mastery was built upon the backs of their animal servants. The humble oxen is slaughtered to feed the masses of Aquilonia, the humble plough horse clears the fields for grain to bake their bread, and sheep provide the wool which is spun to create their finery.

